#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Jippity setup — create config dirs and print KDE hotkey instructions
set -euo pipefail

CONFIG_DIR="${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/jippity"
HISTORY_DIR="${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/jippity"

mkdir -p "$CONFIG_DIR" "$HISTORY_DIR"/{screenshots,responses,logs}

# Default state file if missing
STATE_FILE="$CONFIG_DIR/state"
if [ ! -f "$STATE_FILE" ]; then
    cat > "$STATE_FILE" << EOF
THREAD_ID=""
LAST_MODE=""
CONTINUE_DEFAULT=false
VOICE_ENABLED=false
EOF
fi

SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)"

cat << EOF
Jippity directories created:
  Config:  $CONFIG_DIR
  History: $HISTORY_DIR
  State:   $CONFIG_DIR/state

Dependencies (setup creates directories; it does not install packages):
  - Required: codex, spectacle, kdialog, jq, Python 3, and standard Unix
    commands used by Jippity.
    Some may already be installed depending on your distribution and KDE setup.
  - Recommended: PyQt6 enables a combined input, live-search, tool-access, and continue-thread
    dialog and the history viewer.
    It may already be installed depending on your distribution. Without it,
    ordinary prompts use a two-step kdialog flow and the history viewer is unavailable.
  - Optional voice input (off by default): parecord (or your PipeWire/PulseAudio
    compatibility package), whisper.cpp, and a compatible Whisper model.
    Arch/CachyOS example: paru -S whisper.cpp whisper.cpp-model-small.en
      Enable:  $SCRIPT_DIR/jippity --voice
      Use:     hold Alt (or the on-screen "Hold to Talk" button) while the
               prompt dialog is open. Release to transcribe into the box.
               Edit the transcription before pressing Enter if needed.

To bind KDE global shortcuts:

  1. Open System Settings > Shortcuts > Custom Shortcuts
  2. Add these shortcuts:

     Trigger: Super+S
     Action: Command/URL: $SCRIPT_DIR/jippity --mode region

     Trigger: Super+W
     Action: Command/URL: $SCRIPT_DIR/jippity --mode screen

     Trigger: Super+A
     Action: Command/URL: $SCRIPT_DIR/jippity --mode window

     Trigger: Super+Q
     Action: Command/URL: $SCRIPT_DIR/jippity --mode quick

     Trigger: Super+H
     Action: Command/URL: $SCRIPT_DIR/jippity --history

     Trigger: Super+V
     Action: Command/URL: $SCRIPT_DIR/jippity --voice

Commands:
  $SCRIPT_DIR/jippity --mode <region|screen|window|quick>   Ask a question
  $SCRIPT_DIR/jippity --history                             Browse/search/delete threads, set active
  $SCRIPT_DIR/jippity --voice                               Toggle optional voice input
  $SCRIPT_DIR/jippity-doctor                                Read-only local diagnostics
  $SCRIPT_DIR/jippity-doctor --json                         Structured diagnostics

Doctor checks the supported desktop environment, dependencies, Codex authentication, optional voice
support, Jippity files/state metadata, and active manifests. It does not access
the network, start a Codex conversation, read history contents, or modify any
Jippity data. It may run codex --version and silent codex login status locally,
never makes a model/API request, and never reports authentication details.
Exit codes: 0 required checks pass, 1 required failure, 2 invalid usage.

Optional Codex troubleshooting tool (metadata only; doctor already ships):
  cp "$SCRIPT_DIR/examples/tools/jippity-doctor" "$SCRIPT_DIR/tools/jippity-doctor"
This manifest does not install anything and does not require network access or
unsandboxed execution.

Continue-thread flow:
  - When a thread exists, the dialog shows a "Continue thread" checkbox
  - Default: unchecked (one-off question). Sticky: your last checkbox choice
    is remembered for next time.
  - Check it to send prior conversation context with your new prompt
  - Uncheck it to start a fresh thread

Per-prompt options:
  - "Use live web search" is always available, off by default, and never sticky.
  - "Allow trusted tools full system access" appears only with active tools; it is
    separate from live search, off by default, and never sticky.

History viewer (Super+H):
  - Lists threads (most recent first) with exchange count and timestamp
  - Active thread is marked with ▸ prefix, bold, and a status bar at top
  - Click a thread to read the full transcript
  - Search across prompts and responses
  - Multi-select threads (Ctrl-click) and Delete to remove them and their screenshots
  - "Set as Active Thread" makes the chosen thread active and pre-checks the
    continue checkbox for the next prompt
EOF
